<WikiLayout title="WARDOGS Wiki Editorial Policy" description="Editorial standards for accuracy, sourcing, updates and corrections on WARDOGS Wiki." canonicalPath="/editorial-policy/" pageType="WebPage">
  <h1>WARDOGS Wiki Editorial Policy</h1><p>This policy defines how the Wiki separates confirmed facts, version-bound observations and strategic interpretation. Its purpose is to keep the knowledge database useful without giving uncertain information false authority.</p>
  <h2>Accuracy and attribution</h2><p>Claims should remain proportional to their evidence. Official descriptions can establish a feature or rule, while observed behavior must identify its version and limitations. Strategy is written as guidance, not as a guaranteed outcome.</p>
  <h2>Unconfirmed information</h2><p>If a price, statistic, mechanic or relationship cannot be verified responsibly, it is labeled <strong>Currently unconfirmed</strong>. Editors should not fill gaps by copying an unattributed number, estimating from an image or treating a third-party label as official.</p>
  <h2>Entity and relationship standards</h2><p>Every entity record should connect to at least three useful internal destinations, such as its collection, a comparison, a guide or a related system. Relationships must help readers understand context; they must not imply a mechanical interaction that has not been established.</p>
  <h2>Updates</h2><p>Version-sensitive pages identify their snapshot and are reviewed when documented patches change relevant systems. Patch history records the context of a meaningful review without pretending that unchanged entries were retested after every minor update.</p>
  <h2>Corrections</h2><p>Incorrect or outdated claims are corrected at the source entry so database pages, entity relationships and guides remain aligned. A correction should preserve the stable URL whenever possible and avoid breaking existing internal links.</p>
  <h2>Images and generated media</h2><p>Images must match the page topic and use descriptive alt text. Generated database art is decorative, contains no claimed game data, and must not be presented as an authentic gameplay screenshot. Watermarks, unrelated brand marks and misleading composites are excluded.</p>
  <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Can a guide contain opinion?</h3><p>Yes, when it is framed as strategy and kept separate from confirmed mechanics.</p><h3>Does an unknown field block publication?</h3><p>No. The page can publish with the field marked <strong>Currently unconfirmed</strong> when the remaining content is useful and accurate.</p>
</WikiLayout>
